      "description": "MaxSAT is the problem of the finding the maximum number of clauses which can be satisfied for a particular formula. MaxSAT can be seen as an optimisation version of the SAT problem. Minimally Unsatisfiable Subformulas (MUSs) are like duals MaxSAT, they ask for the minimal set of assignments which will show a formula is unsatisfiable. - wiki\nSolvers include:",
