      "description": "Satisfiable Modulo Theory (SMT) solvers are generally built on top of SAT solvers and make use of expressive theories such as bit-vectors and or uninterpreted functions. SMT solvers generally use an extension of the DPLL algorithm called DPLL(T) (T is for Theory) | wiki\nSolvers include:",
